<header class="sp-head"><p class="featured-region">8 November 1519 · Tenochtitlan</p><h1 class="sp-title">Moctezuma Greets Cortés</h1><p class="sp-by"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moctezuma-ii">Moctezuma II</a></p></header>
<section class="sp-sec"><h2>The setting</h2><p>Having marched inland from the Gulf coast with a few hundred Spaniards and thousands of Indigenous allies, above all from Tlaxcala, Hernán Cortés reached Tenochtitlan, the island capital of the Mexica, in November 1519. The ruler Moctezuma II came out on the causeway to meet him and lodged the Spaniards in his father's palace. Cortés later reported a speech of welcome that Moctezuma made to him there.</p></section>
<section class="sp-sec"><h2>In substance</h2><p class="sp-para">Our ancestors came to this land from far away, led by a lord who later departed, and we have always believed that his descendants would one day return to rule us. Since you come from where the sun rises and speak of a great lord who sent you, we take him to be our natural lord, and we will obey you in his place.</p><p class="sp-source">A summary of the speech as Cortés reported it to Charles V in his Second Letter (1520). Historians doubt it: Cortés needed to show that Moctezuma had handed over his realm lawfully, and the Mexica's own accounts tell the meeting differently.</p></section>
<section class="sp-sec"><h2>What followed</h2><p>Within a week Moctezuma was a prisoner in his own city. He died in June 1520 during the uprising against the Spaniards, who were driven out with heavy losses on the Noche Triste. Cortés returned with his Indigenous allies and, after a siege of nearly three months, took Tenochtitlan in August 1521, ending the Aztec Empire.</p><div class="sp-led"><h3 class="sp-led-k">What it led to</h3><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-noche-triste">La Noche Triste</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fall-of-tenochtitlan">Fall of Tenochtitlan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-conquest-of-the-aztec-empire">Spanish conquest of the Aztec Empire</a></div></div></section>
